A||N||3||anthony_86gt||rear speakers, HELP!!||||8||
Z||000000||anthony_86gt||02-11-2001||08:31 PM||||I was about to install new 4x6s and i ran into a problem.  i ripped off the speaker covers and they broke off. what can i do to cover the speakers??  and how in the heck do you remove the speakers??? please help me fix my problems. <P>i have a 86.5 gt  ||||reg||8
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-11-2001||08:43 PM||||You are not supposed to take off the speaker covers from the outside.  You have to remove that entire panel there to get at the speakers.  You'll have to take off the lower inside plastic molding, and then the seatbelt assemblies (you'll need a T-47 torx bit for these), and then carefully remove the plastic panels.  Then you'll be able to get at the speakers.  I also took out my seats when I installed my speakers, it just made it a lot easier to move around.<P>Once you have the panel off, you'll probably be able to glue on the speaker cover that you broke off with super glue.<P>Good luck!<P>btw - What kind of speakers did you get?<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||02-11-2001||10:14 PM||||Yes the entire panel has to come off. To repair the speaker grills I would suggest 5-minute epoxy and a metal washer with a small screw. I have fixed then before that way.||||reg||1
Z||000003||anthony_86gt||02-12-2001||05:54 PM||||Thanks so much for the help!!!  Geez you guys reply quick!  I got Pioneer 3-ways, at 65w.  They sound good enough for 4x6s.  Thanks again!||||reg||10
